# TypeScript

- `strict: true`. No `any` at HTTP, DB, or env boundaries. No `as` to silence the checker without a one-line reason.
- ESM: `"type": "module"`. Relative imports use the `.js` specifier (`../config/env.js`).
- Type every exported function. Prefer `T | null` over optional bag types for “missing row”.

## Naming

| Element | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Files | `{resource}.ts` inside the layer folder (`src/services/products.ts`) |
| Types / classes | PascalCase |
| Functions / variables | camelCase |
| Env / constants | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` |
| Tables (Drizzle export) | camelCase plural (`products`) |

## Errors and I/O

- Catch specific errors; never empty `catch`. Re-throw with `cause` preserved (`throw new AppError(..., { cause })` or `from`).
- No `fs.readFileSync`, `child_process.execSync`, or other blocking I/O on the request path.
- No `console.log` in application code — use the pino logger.
- Express 5 types `req.params` / `req.query` as `string | string[]`. After `validate`, coerce with `String(req.params.id)` (or parse with Zod and assign to a local).

## Tooling

`typescript-eslint` + `tsc --noEmit`. No `eslint-disable` or `@ts-expect-error` without an inline explanation. Defer libraries to `stack.mdc`.
